Subject: Controller menus: the D-pad and sticks move between menu buttons
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The game's menus are pointer-only. With controller menus on (a [gameplay]
tweak), a gamepad player moves between a menu's buttons with the D-pad and the
sticks instead, as in the Strikers WiiCompiled port: the pointer snaps onto
the next button that way, so the game's own hand marks the selection and its
hover and press logic run unchanged. B goes to the screen's back button and
presses it, and the triggers turn pages. The port decides where the pointer
goes (src/platform/controller_menus.cpp, mscharged_tweak_navigate_menu).

PlatPadManager::UpdateChannel calls FENavigateMenus (feDPD.cpp) for each
Nunchuk remote it reads. For a channel the port navigates, it gathers the
menu's live buttons: the registered pointer listeners, enabled and not locked
out, whose last event for that channel is at its pointer. Scenes pass pointer
events only to the screens they show, so the buttons of registered but hidden
screens drop out; the character grids of the captain and sidekick scenes stay
live while hidden and are left out by hand. It then writes the pointer the
port asks for into the reading (KPAD's position, GetPointerPosition's mapping
the other way round), adds its presses (A, 1, + and -) to the remote's buttons
and hides or shows the hand. Hiding gives the hand's instances a transparent
colour override and puts their own back after.

Two helpers have no original counterpart: FEPointerRegion's turn and pivot
are read for a turned button's middle, and back buttons are counted as they
are made and destroyed (FEIsBackButton), as the build has no RTTI.

